Determining which path a router could take

Things to consider:
    Believablility of a route

        Since routers can support multiple protocols at once, we have to decide which protocol to go with based one certain factors

        Routers use an index of believability --> Administratice Distance (AD)

        Lower AD is considered more believable/trustworthy

        Believable ---> less Believable

        Directly Connected --> Statically Connected --> EIGRP --> OSPF --> RIP


    Metrics associated with each of the routes
        - Hop count         - Delay         - Believability         - Costs
        - Reliability       - Bandwidth     - Other metrics

        Each protocol uses a different metric depending on what it considers faster or slower

        Lower metrics are preferred over higher metrics